le=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span=
 style=3D"font-weight:700">A satisfying need for force</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>A=
=2EI. is rapidly becoming superhuman at tasks with clear solutions like cod=
ing and math. The more I use A.I. =E2=80=94 and I use it a lot =E2=80=94 th=
e more I worry about surrendering my cognition. A study published in Nature=
 this year found that researchers who used A.I. assistance tended to be mor=
e productive than their peers but also studied fewer new topics.</span></p>=
<p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"=
><span>My analog moment arrived in early 2025. I opened Gmail, began to com=
pose an email reply and noticed a full potential draft generated by A.I., l=
ike an apparition from an undesired future.</span></p><p style=3D"font:norm=
al 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>This bland, sy=
nthetic reply was an assault to my creative flow, interrupting my train of =
thought with some statistical average of soulless prose. Around the same ti=
me, Google Docs automatically enabled A.I. writing suggestions in its Works=
pace accounts, and Apple brought its own version of intelligent autocomplet=
e to computers and phones. I felt betrayed, deprived of opportunities to th=
ink, uninhibited, for myself.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px g=
eorgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>So that May, I bought an old=
 Olivetti from Goodwill=E2=80=99s online auction house.</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>T=
he keys were gummy and almost impossible to press. But after a few late nig=
hts watching maintenance videos on YouTube, I learned the basic cleaning ri=
tuals that often loosen up neglected typewriters. After a modest cleanse, t=
he machine sprang to life with crisp, responsive action.</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>T=
he keys still required much more force than my MacBook=E2=80=99s one-millim=
eter keyboard, but as a lifelong pianist, I found the action incredibly sat=
isfying. My keystrokes crescendoed as I excitedly unearthed words that mode=
rn tech had stopped me from digging up. There is a certain violence to usin=
g a typewriter, firing hammers into a ribbon of ink with enough force to im=
print a page. Some writing ought to be more violent, more evocative, more e=
xpressive. Otherwise it might blend in with the timidity of much A.I. prose=
=2E</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;ma=
rgin:0 0 15px"><span>The typewriter is a technology that is perfect for wha=
t it needs to do: a co-pilot that speeds up your work but keeps you in cont=
rol of your own thoughts. In an era of overly rapid technological progress,=
 that feels just right.</span></p><table border=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cel=
